<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Augustus II the Strong</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1670">1670</a>–1733</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Augustus II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Augustus II the Strong was Elector of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> and King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and Grand Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>, ruling for most of the period from 1697 to 1733. His involvement in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-northern-war">Great Northern War</a> brought Swedish invasion and devastation to the Commonwealth, and he was temporarily deposed. His reign saw growing Russian influence and weakening of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/augustus-ii-the-strong.jpg" alt="Augustus II the Strong" width="314" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Louis de Silvestre · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Louis_de_Silvestre-August_II.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
